 {r}←{storm}WriteToWindowsEvents (parms crash);msg;note;full
⍝ `storm` is the storm guard's note and whether the crash gets the full treatment; defaults to '' 1.
⍝ Without the full treatment there are no details in the error folder, so the event does not point there.
 r←⍬
 storm←{0=⎕NC ⍵:'' 1 ⋄ ⍎⍵}'storm'
 (note full)←storm
 :If 'Win'≡APLTreeUtils2.GetOperatingSystem ⍬
 :AndIf 0≠≢parms.windowsEventSource
     :Trap (parms.trapInternalErrors)/0
         msg←⊂'Application has crashed, RC=',(⍕crash.EN),'; MSG=',crash.EM
         msg,←(full∧0<≢parms.errorFolder)/''('Details can be found in ',parms.errorFolder)
         :If 0≠≢parms.addToMsg
             msg,←{(≡⍵)∊0 1:,⊂,⍵ ⋄ ⍵}parms.addToMsg
         :EndIf
         :If 0≠≢note
             msg,←⊂note
         :EndIf
         ReportErrorToWindowsLog parms.windowsEventSource msg
     :EndTrap
 :EndIf
